const audit=`<p><span class="badge source">Actual embedded data</span> ${D.research.length} research technologies, ${D.trees.length} tree definitions and ${D.buildings.length} building records. The original retains client costs, cumulative benefits, raw durations and structured prerequisites. All records are preserved in this dashboard.</p><p><strong>Original controls:</strong> numeric ROI inputs, research level/held/availability edits, a searchable invoice ledger and manual JSON export/import. No localStorage persistence, editable building account, dependency scheduler, resource forecast or actual charts were present. Construction state and route totals were prose, so research edits could not update those totals.</p><p><strong>Calculation audit:</strong> marginal speed and production formulas were structurally sound, but null inputs correctly left much of the output unknown. Speed ranking mixed separate queues through a screening ratio; it was not a calendar ROI. The old import checked only a few top-level keys, and imports/edits were not automatically saved. Research held flags defaulted to false even though the notes said the held inventory was unknown; this dashboard treats unreviewed status as unknown.</p><p><strong>Known limitations:</strong> screenshot interpretations and approximate inventory are last known, not live verified. Economy 93% and Prosperous Economy 41% cannot identify individual levels. Building costs omit additional live reductions, future troop training and protected combat budgets. The corrected T9 path is user-specified: Base 27 → Camp 1 27. Added client Camp costs come from the existing saved progression snapshot, id 1020. Live troop unlock thresholds for the other camps remain unknown. Source URLs are provenance; no live-source refresh was performed.</p>`;
